We are looking for a Middle+ SDET to join our active team supporting a SaaS platform automating compliance workflows for financial firms. The role combines UI/API automation with Playwright and TypeScript, CI/CD quality engineering in Azure DevOps, and observability in Grafana across multi-tenant cloud and broker-integration sub-teams.
Requirements:

• 3+ years of hands-on experience as an SDET or QA Automation Engineer on SaaS products;

• Strong proficiency in TypeScript and building UI/API test frameworks with Playwright;

• Solid experience testing RESTful APIs, microservices, and data-ingestion pipelines;

• Hands-on experience integrating automated tests into Azure DevOps CI/CD pipelines;

• Practical experience with Grafana for monitoring logs, metrics, and test trends;

• Strong SQL, debugging skills, and Upper-intermediate English.

Responsibilities:

• Build and maintain UI, API, and E2E test suites using Playwright and TypeScript in Visual Studio Code;

• Use AI coding agents (including Claude Code) to accelerate test authoring and maintenance;

• Automate validation for personal trading, holdings monitoring, and compliance workflows;

• Develop integration tests for third-party brokerage statement ingestion pipelines;

• Maintain test runs in Azure DevOps pipelines and track stability in Grafana;

• Troubleshoot failures across cloud environments and validate new AI-driven features.

Nice to Have:

• Experience using Claude Code or similar AI coding tools in daily workflows;

• FinTech or regulatory compliance background (SEC, FCA, MiFID II);

• Hands-on experience with Microsoft Azure and/or AWS;

• Experience testing multi-tenant SaaS architectures or LLM-based features.

